IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tma-types`

-- Taxes Management Act 1970 (UK) — GOAL 3: ASSESSMENT TIME LIMITS (ss 34,
-- 36, 36A).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1970-9.txt.

§ `Goal 3 — assessment time limits`

-- s 34(1): "not more than 4 years after the end of the year of assessment";
-- s 36(1): careless, 6 years; s 36A(2): offshore matter or transfer, 12
-- years (subject to s 36(1A)); s 36(1A): deliberate, a s 7 failure, or a
-- scheme disclosure failure, 20 years. The year ends on 5 April Y+1.
@ref ss 34(1), 36(1)-(1A), 36A(2)
@export The last day on which HMRC may make an income tax or capital gains tax assessment under ss 34, 36 and 36A of the Taxes Management Act 1970 (UK): 5 April 4 years after the end of the tax year; 6 years for a careless loss of tax; 12 years for a loss involving an offshore matter or transfer; 20 years for a deliberate loss, a s 7 failure, or a scheme disclosure failure. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER     @desc The tax year, by the calendar year it begins in
      loss IS A `Loss of tax` @desc How any loss of tax was brought about
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for an assessment for` year `where the loss is` loss MEANS
    Date 5 4 (year PLUS 1 PLUS n)
    WHERE
        n MEANS
            CONSIDER loss
            WHEN `no loss brought about by the taxpayer` THEN 4
            WHEN `careless` THEN 6
            WHEN `involving an offshore matter or transfer` THEN 12
            WHEN `deliberate, a section 7 failure, or a scheme disclosure failure` THEN 20
